<title>USA: U.S. Sept durable goods orders rose 4.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Sept durable goods orders rose 4.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on durable goods orders, with percent changes from prior months.</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:     Sept     Aug--Rev from    July</p>
<p>  New Orders		  4.6    -3.5    -3.2	 1.4</p>
<p>  Transportation Equip.  17.5    -8.8    -7.9	-1.5</p>
<p>  NonTransport.Equip.     0.9    -1.8    -1.6	 2.4</p>
<p>  NonDefense Orders	 4.5    -3.7    -3.6	 3.5</p>
<p>  Defense Cap Orders	7.9     2.0    10.0     -40.7</p>
<p>  NonDefense Cap Orders  14.1   -10.4   -10.2	 7.0</p>
<p>  -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts    3.1    -4.9    -5.0	 3.7</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    Sept   August--Rev from    July</p>
<p> New Orders		174.06   166.36   166.80    172.40</p>
<p> Transportation Equip.  44.07    37.51    37.89     41.13</p>
<p> NonTransport.Equip.   129.99   128.85   129.14    131.28</p>
<p> NonDefense Orders     168.77   161.45   161.51    167.60</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders	5.29     4.90     5.29	4.81</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders  46.98    41.17    41.26     45.94</p>
<p> -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   37.98    36.84    36.81     38.76</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:     Sept     Aug--Rev from    July</p>
<p> Total Shipments	    1.4     0.4     0.3	 0.5</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders    0.7    -0.4    -0.3	 1.0</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    Sept   August--Rev from   July</p>
<p> Total Shipments	 170.80   168.50  168.24    167.77</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders   481.15   477.89  478.59    480.03</p>
<p> NEW ORDERS-PCT CHANGES  Sept     Aug--Rev from    July</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	   -1.7    -4.0    -2.6	 1.6</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery   -0.9    -0.8    -0.7	 2.8</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery    1.9    -5.2    -5.6	 4.9</p>
<p>NEW ORDERS-BILLIONS OF DLRS:</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	  14.91    15.16   15.39     15.80</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery  32.05    32.34   32.36     32.59</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery  27.14    26.62   26.49     28.07</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected September durable goods orders to rise 2.0 percent. Excluding defense orders, they expected a 1.3 percent increase.</p>
<p>September's 4.6 percent rise in durable goods orders was the largest since a 7.8 percent increase in December 1992, the department said.</p>
<p>It said the 4.5 percent gain in orders excluding defense was the largest since December 1992's 8.2 percent increase.</p>
<p>The 0.9 percent increase in durables orders excluding transportation was the fifth rise in the last six months.</p>
